# Umami analytics: the tracker URL and each board's website id, in ONE place.
#
# Committed rather than held as GitHub repo variables, because that is exactly
# what broke. The tracker URL was a variable naming the analytics subdomain of
# the old single-app box; the box became jacobanana/mixedmode-deploy, where
# analytics is a platform service on its own domain, and the bundle went on
# asking for a hostname nothing serves any more. Nothing errors when that
# happens - the script 404s, every track() stays a no-op, and the dashboard
# just shows no traffic. A value that has to track another repo's `sites` map
# belongs in a diff, not in a settings page nobody re-reads.
#
# Every value here is public: they ship in the page source as the tracker's
# src and its data-website-id. Nothing secret goes in this file.
#
# Read by .github/workflows/publish.yml (the self-hosted web image) and
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml (the GitHub Pages build). Both grep it rather
# than sourcing it - it is data, not a shell script. It is in publish.yml's
# `web` path filter, so editing it rebuilds and redeploys the web image.
#
# Registering a site is a dashboard action in Umami; the id it hands back goes
# here. Running Umami is the deploy repo's business (stacks/umami).

# Where the tracker script is served from. The hostname must match
# ANALYTICS_ADDRESS in the deploy repo's terraform/variables.tf `sites` map -
# one declaration there provisions the A record and tells Caddy what to answer
# on, and this is the client half of the same fact.
UMAMI_SRC=https://analytics.mixedmode.ch/script.js

# The maths board, mathsboard.mixedmode.ch.
UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=b16779cd-dc0c-499b-b2a7-9532062952d8

# The language board, langsboard.mixedmode.ch. Its OWN site: the two boards are
# separate products on separate domains, and one shared id would blend a maths
# lesson into the language board's reports and make neither answerable.
UMAMI_LANGUAGE_WEBSITE_ID=eb6fd4be-dc1d-4054-a0fa-40006bdc6598

# The public GitHub Pages build is a third site, and its id stays the
# UMAMI_PAGES_WEBSITE_ID repo variable (deploy.yml). It is one origin serving
# both boards, so it reports as one site - which is also why the frontend falls
# back to a single id when no language id is set (src/analytics.ts).
